<Layout>
  <h1>an archive of <span class="proper">tora vyl drak</span></h1>

  <p class="lede">
    a world built inside a volcanic caldera, twenty-five hundred years after the sky fell — its people, its places, its language, and the long quiet history that shaped them.
  </p>

  <hr class="kahu-rule" />

  <p>
    in the year 4625 of the old calendar, the <span class="proper">kahu</span> live inside an eighteen-mile caldera in the bones of the cascade range. they call their home <span class="proper">tora vyl drak</span> — <em>the call of life, the place of the long ones</em> — though most of them have forgotten the older meaning of <span class="kt">drak</span>. the world above the rim is <span class="kt">peli-shen</span>, danger-life, a fungal sea that took the lowlands when the comet broke and the bombs fell. the world below is the <span class="proper">kahu</span>: roughly two hundred and seventy-eight thousand people, woven into a tapestry of smaller kahu, tending each other and the systems that keep them alive.
  </p>

  <p>
    this is the encyclopedia of that world. it is being written, slowly, by hand. the voice here is objective — a record. stories told from inside the world live elsewhere.
  </p>

